# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  'SNYK-JS-BRACES-19963945':
    - 'nodemon > chokidar > braces':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on nodemon@3.1.14 > chokidar@3.6.0 > braces@3.0.3: braces@3.0.3. Stack exhaustion requires deeply nested attacker-controlled brace patterns. The development watcher/build/stylelint paths take patterns from repository files and CLI configuration, not applicant form values; they do not run in the server request path. No fixed braces release exists. Remove when upstream drops braces or a fixed release is published; reassess if pattern sources change.'
        expires: '2026-12-05'
  'SNYK-JS-DEEPMERGE-19964053':
    - 'jest > @jest/core > jest-config > deepmerge':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on jest@30.5.2 > jest-config@30.5.2 > deepmerge@4.3.1. Prototype replacement needs an attacker-controlled source object containing __proto__ passed to mergeObject(). Jest uses deepmerge for repository-controlled test configuration, presets and globals; applicant input does not reach these configuration merges. Development dependency, outside server requests. No fixed deepmerge release exists. Remove when Jest drops or fixes deepmerge; reassess if test configuration becomes untrusted.'
        expires: '2026-12-05'
  'SNYK-JS-INFLIGHT-6095116':
    - '@pact-foundation/pact > @pact-foundation/pact-core > pino-pretty > help-me > glob > inflight':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on @pact-foundation/pact@15.0.1 > @pact-foundation/pact-core@16.1.1 > pino-pretty@9.4.1 > help-me@4.2.0 > glob@8.1.0 > inflight@1.0.6: inflight@1.0.6. The leak requires repeated asynchronous operations through inflight. This development path scans repository source files or the Pact logger''s installed help directory during build/test/CLI execution, not applicant input or server requests. No fixed inflight release exists. Remove when upstream drops legacy glob/inflight or a compatible fix is published.'
        expires: '2026-12-05'
  'SNYK-JS-MINIMATCH-22111072':
    - 'eslint > @eslint/config-array > minimatch':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on eslint@9.39.5 > @eslint/config-array@0.21.2 > minimatch@3.1.5: minimatch@3.1.5. Amplification requires attacker-controlled patterns with optimizationLevel >= 2; installed minimatch v3/v5 has neither firstPhasePreProcess nor optimizationLevel. These callers use repository-controlled lint, build, package-script or help-file patterns. Fixed v11.0.3 cleared seven-day cooldown on 2026-11-04T20:00:34.713Z, but its object exports replace the callable API used by legacy callers. Modern v7+ paths are overridden to v11.0.3. Remove when upstream adopts a compatible fixed release; reassess if callers or pattern sources change.'
