    - 'eslint > @eslint/eslintrc > ajv > uri-js':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on eslint@9.39.5 > @eslint/eslintrc@3.3.7 > ajv@6.15.0 > uri-js@4.4.1. Exploitation requires attacker-controlled malformed percent-encoded URIs reaching pctDecChars and downstream use of decoded metacharacters. Ajv resolves repository-controlled ESLint configuration schema identifiers; applicant input does not reach those URIs. Development tooling, outside server requests. No fixed uri-js release exists. Remove when ESLint drops uri-js or a compatible fix is published; reassess if configuration sources change.'
